# Ignore rules for the disposable spike repository.
#
# ⚠ This file matters more here than it looks. ADR-001 §8.3 rule 7's
# protections are ON for this repository — protected `main`, no force-push,
# linear history — so anything that reaches this history CANNOT be removed
# from it. Rule 7 says so in its own words: "a history that cannot be
# rewritten cuts both ways: nothing can be removed from it either."
#
# The repository is also PUBLIC. Both facts together mean a careless commit
# is not a tidying problem, it is a delete-and-recreate problem.

# --- dependencies: the one that would be unfixable ---
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# --- Expo / React Native generated output ---
# android/ and ios/ are produced by `expo prebuild` (continuous native
# generation), so they are build output rather than source for this spike.
.expo/
android/
ios/
dist/
web-build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- built application packages ---
# 🔴 These can embed signing material, and this repository is public.
# D5's discipline is a development identity that is separately revocable and
# a distribution certificate that never leaves the owner's keychain — an
# .apk/.ipa committed here would defeat both.
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.app
*.dSYM.zip

# --- credentials and secrets ---
# Signing material is received as an injected secret and nothing is retained
# after the build (ADR-012 §3a rule 1). Nothing of the sort belongs in-tree.
.env
.env.*
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# --- the provenance list, belt and braces ---
# It lives at .git/provenance-forbidden.txt, which git never commits, so this
# is redundant by design. Kept because rule 7's whole point is that the list
# must not reach the repository, and a redundant guard costs nothing.
provenance-forbidden.txt

# --- Rust build output (the ADR-005 §4.4a evaluator) ---
# `target/` is a compiler cache, and a large one. `Cargo.lock` IS tracked, for
# the same reason `package-lock.json` is: `D1` pins packages "by name and
# version" because a p95 that gates an ADR has to be reproducible.
evaluator/target/

# `SC-10`'s cross-compiled artefacts — BUILD OUTPUT, generated in CI before
# prebuild and never committed. ⚠ A 23 MB archive per ABI in a public
# repository with unrewritable history would be the one mistake `.gitignore`
# cannot undo, which is what the header above this file is about.
modules/antarii-evaluator/android/src/main/jniLibs/
modules/antarii-evaluator/ios/*.a

# --- measurement output ---
# Figures belong in the record (§8), not in the history as raw dumps.
/measurements/
*.measurements.json

# --- noise ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
